# THE UNITAS GLOBAL — sovereign attestation line-ending pin.
#
# config/security/trust-registry.json pins the sha256 of each file below, and
# web/scripts/trust-registry.mjs hashes RAW BYTES:
#   createHash('sha256').update(readFileSync(abs))
# There is no CRLF normalization in that hash, by design — the registry must
# detect any byte-level change to a script that runs unattended on this machine.
#
# This repository is checked out with core.autocrlf=true. Without the pins
# below, `git clone` / `git checkout` expands the LF blobs in the index into
# CRLF in the working tree, every pinned hash mismatches, `trust-registry
# --verify` fails closed, and the Codex 제15장 3단계 idle sweep refuses to run
# on a machine where nothing is actually wrong. Measured and reproduced
# 2026-09-16 (9/13 pins mismatched immediately after a checkout).
#
# Keep this narrow: it pins only the attested surface, so it cannot renormalize
# the rest of the tree.
web/scripts/** text eol=lf
config/security/trust-registry.json text eol=lf
